  "text": "Only if you look suspicious do you get the visible challenge, a completely automated public Turing test to tell computers and humans apart, or simply a CAPTCHA. Classic ones asked you to label images, which conveniently generated training data for computer vision models. The bar keeps rising because AI now solves the old ones. The bar keeps rising because AI now solves the old ones. It's an arms race. The same vision models that read street signs for self-driving cars can also solve image CAPTCHAs, so defenses keep shifting towards behavior and device signals. You proving you're human is also teaching machines to see. Next episode, we'll learn why you never get charged twice",
